
 Bob,

    I wouldn't want you to get desperate. I've knocked up a quick example for you that I believe is usable. You'll have to copy it to your OPL editor and translate it. It also is a good (I hope) example of how to use FRC:. There are some long lines here, so open your window wide when viewing.

 -------------------------------------------

 Proc Frc:
 local h%,start%,can%,read%
 local pmode%,arg&
 local hr%,m%,s%,k%,fon%,mywin%
 local hr$(2),mn$(2),sec$(4)

 rem Pelican Software Inc.
 rem The FRC: device driver can only be used by one program at a time.
 rem The accuracy is to the 1/1024 of a second.
 rem I wrote this quickly, so it may not be perfect. I think it is
 rem accurate though, and I haven't gotten any errors when running it.

 start%=15    rem P_FSTART
 can%=4       rem P_FCANCEL
 read%=1      rem P_FREAD
 pmode%=0     rem E_FRC_COUNTING

 guse 1 :gsetwin 0,0,0,0
 mywin%=gcreate(0,0,480,160,1,1)       rem need a grey window for buttons
 fon%=gloadfont("ROM::sa37snd.fon")    rem use nice numbers
 gfont fon%
 IOOPEN(h%,"FRC:",-1)                  rem open FRC: dev driver
 start::
 IOW(h%,can%,#0,#0)                    rem cancel for next time around
 IOW(h%,start%,pmode%,#0)              rem P_FSTART
 cls
 giprint "FRC: Device Driver open"
 gfont 7
 gat 145,100 :gbutton "Elapsed",1,80,25,0    rem must have buttons
 gat 260,100 :gbutton "Stop",1,80,25,0
 top::
 gfont fon%
 do
    IOW(h%,read%,arg&,#0)        rem P_FREAD
    hr$=right$("00"+fix$(arg&/1024.0/1024.0/1024.0,0,3),2)
    mn$=right$("00"+fix$(arg&/1024.0/1024.0,0,3),2)
    s%=arg&/1024.0
    sec$=right$("0000"+fix$(arg&-(int(arg&/1024.0)*1024.0),0,4),4)
    gat 5,70
    gprintb hr$+":"+mn$+":"+right$("00"+fix$(int(arg&/1024.0),0,4),2)+"."+sec$,gwidth-1 0,3
    k%=key
 until k%=%e or k%=%s or k%=27
 gfont 7
 press:(k%)
 if k%=%e
    gat 5,150
    gprintb"(Elapsed: "+hr$+":"+mn$+":"+right$("00"+fix$(int(arg&/1024.0),0,4),2)+"."+sec$+")",gw idth-10,3
    goto top
 endif
 IOCLOSE(h%)
 Endp

 Proc press:(k%)
 if k%=%s or k%=%S
    gat 260,100 :gbutton "Stop",1,80,25,2
    pause 3
    gat 260,100 :gbutton "Stop",1,80,25,0
 elseif k%=%e or k%=%E
    gat 145,100 :gbutton "Elapsed",1,80,25,2
    pause 3
    gat 145,100 :gbutton "Elapsed",1,80,25,0
 endif
 Endp


  -Mark Esposito
